Human: Can you tell me the steps to write an if/then statement in C programming language?

Assistant: Sure, that’s an if...then...else statement, the same as in other programming languages. Here’s an example with three conditions:

if (x > 10) {
    cout << "Good morning, Mr. X!" << endl;
}

or in C++:

if (x > 10) {
    cout << "Good morning, Mr. X!" << endl;
}

or even in JavaScript:

if (x > 10) {
    console.log("Good morning, Mr. X!");
}

and you can be more specific if you use nested conditions:

if (x > 10) {
    if (y > 20) {
        console.log("Good morning, Mr. X!");
    } else {
        console.log("Hello, Mr. Y!");
    }
}
